6. Verification and Assurance Claims

A passing producer self-test, browser test, parity result, property result, tamper result, independent reconstruction result, frozen corpus result, checksum result, capsule result, or other verification result applies only to the declared files, profiles, inputs, corpora, rules, manifests, evidence, canonicalization, and verification boundary associated with that result.

Modified files, changed rules, changed profiles, changed corpora, changed manifests, changed evidence, changed inputs, changed canonicalization, or changed verification artifacts require their own verification.

Redistribution, modification, or use of the covered materials must not imply third-party verification, certification, production qualification, legal approval, security approval, safety approval, domain validation, or endorsement by the original project maintainers unless such status has been separately and explicitly established.

7. System Boundary and Responsibility

ORL-AI is a deterministic decision-admission reference system for bounded declared structure. It is not a trained model, general artificial intelligence system, truth detector, source-authentication system, model-independence detector, consensus protocol, authorization system, or execution engine.

The materials do not guarantee prediction accuracy, factual truth, source authenticity, declared source independence, model safety, legal validity, regulatory compliance, security, availability, fitness for a particular domain, or correctness of real-world action.

A `RESOLVED` state means only that one candidate satisfied the declared ORL-AI profile and ruleset within the admitted boundary. `INCOMPLETE`, `ABSTAIN`, `DENIED`, and `REFUSED` are bounded structural states and do not independently establish safety.

The field `authority = NONE` means the reference result does not grant execution authority.

Users are responsible for domain validation, source authentication, evidence quality, policy design, security controls, human oversight where required, legal compliance, and all consequences of deployment or use.

